---
import SectionHeader from '../ui/SectionHeader.astro'
import Substrate from '../marketing/Substrate.astro'
---

<section id="developers" class="border-b border-border py-12 lg:py-14">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <SectionHeader
      title="Build on the same data"
      subtitle="xNet’s substrate is the data layer under the app. Like Lego pieces, its records share a common fit: you can combine them, extend them, and build a different tool around them."
    />
    <Substrate />
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-5 text-sm font-medium">
      <a href="/docs/quickstart/" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline dark:text-indigo-400">
        Quickstart →
      </a>
      <a href="/build-with" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline dark:text-indigo-400">
        SDKs & languages →
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/clutch-power" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline dark:text-indigo-400">
        Why the pieces fit: Clutch Power →
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
      The alpha SDK is available today. A wider ecosystem of interchangeable tools is the
      longer-term goal.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
